          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mryyhdgovt6eudk6",
          "message": {
            "text": "This is the whole demotion mechanism: a demoted region's text is forced INELIGIBLE at the single eligibility gate, so strip (the chrome clone) leaves its textSegments in the chrome tree instead of the glyph layer — the exact path occluded / decorated / complex-script text already takes, which is why it's pixel-safe by the same argument. ctx.region here is the region an element's OWN text buckets into (set at the declared/isRegionRoot branch just above; the clipping-region update below only affects CHILDREN), so it matches the region stamped on the glyphs and returned in CompressedRunResult.regions — the key the guard trials. Demoting every region is the whole chrome union (the whole-run fallback).\n",
            "markdown": "This is the whole demotion mechanism: a demoted region's text is forced INELIGIBLE at the single eligibility gate, so `strip` (the chrome clone) leaves its `textSegments` in the chrome tree instead of the glyph layer — the exact path occluded / decorated / complex-script text already takes, which is why it's pixel-safe by the same argument. `ctx.region` here is the region an element's OWN text buckets into (set at the declared/isRegionRoot branch just above; the clipping-region update below only affects CHILDREN), so it matches the `region` stamped on the glyphs and returned in `CompressedRunResult.regions` — the key the guard trials. Demoting every region is the whole chrome union (the whole-run fallback).\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/animation/compressed-run.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 598,
                  "endLine": 598,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    if (elementTextEligible(el, ctx) && !occluded(el) && !demoted.has(ctx.region)) {"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
