      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "ms0e22mw8goza9sf",
          "message": {
            "text": "Root cause of the cross-line garble was NOT the bucket/glyph pairing (that pairs correctly — verified by instrumenting pairBuckets: bar@y85 → ready@y85, same line). It's here in groupElement: the compressor's single-line render anchors the baseline on the element's textTop, but a CapturedElement carries ONE textTop — the top of its FIRST text segment. When one element has same-color text nodes on several lines (a <div white-space:pre> with \\ns, e.g. a terminal body), a glyph group born on a LATER line inherited the first line's textTop and rendered stacked on line 1. The old textTop += dyTotal only corrected the group's own cross-line MOVE, not the offset between the group's birth line and the element's first segment. The (first.ys[0] - firstSegY) term adds that offset; for a single-line source firstSegY === first.ys[0] so it's 0 and every existing golden is byte-identical (verified: 26/26). Regression test + mutant check in compressed-run.e2e.test.ts.\n",
            "markdown": "Root cause of the cross-line garble was NOT the bucket/glyph pairing (that pairs correctly — verified by instrumenting `pairBuckets`: bar@y85 → ready@y85, same line). It's here in `groupElement`: the compressor's single-line render anchors the baseline on the element's `textTop`, but a `CapturedElement` carries ONE `textTop` — the top of its FIRST text segment. When one element has same-color text nodes on several lines (a `<div white-space:pre>` with `\\n`s, e.g. a terminal body), a glyph group born on a LATER line inherited the first line's textTop and rendered stacked on line 1. The old `textTop += dyTotal` only corrected the group's own cross-line MOVE, not the offset between the group's birth line and the element's first segment. The `(first.ys[0] - firstSegY)` term adds that offset; for a single-line source `firstSegY === first.ys[0]` so it's 0 and every existing golden is byte-identical (verified: 26/26). Regression test + mutant check in compressed-run.e2e.test.ts.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/animation/compressed-run.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1071,
                  "endLine": 1071,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    const firstSegY = first.rec.srcEl.textSegments?.[0]?.y ?? first.ys[0];"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
